cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Reverse metabolomics across public LC-MS/MS repositories: a reproducible
  workflow, applied to tryptophan and kynurenine and to omeprazole and
  5-hydroxyomeprazole
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Philippine
    family-names: Louail
    email: philoulouail@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/philouail/reverse-met"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible six-step workflow (search, metadata, curation,
  confirmation, extraction, analysis) for reusing public LC-MS/MS data at
  scale, built on the RforMassSpectrometry ecosystem. Target compounds are
  searched in FASSTrecords, a database of precomputed MASST matches; the
  deposits that hold them are described from the metadata of MassIVE,
  MetaboLights and the Metabolomics Workbench; their hits are confirmed with
  SIRIUS and CSI:FingerID; and each target's MS1 peak is measured in every
  file of the confirmed assays. Two applications use it: the ratio of
  kynurenine to tryptophan against age in adult blood, and the ratio of
  omeprazole to 5-hydroxyomeprazole, checked against CYP2C19 genotype in a
  dosed cohort.
keywords:
  - metabolomics
  - mass spectrometry
  - reverse metabolomics
  - public data reuse
  - FASSTrecords
  - SIRIUS
  - tryptophan
  - kynurenine
  - pharmacogenomics
  - CYP2C19
  - omeprazole
license: Apache-2.0
